  "notes" : "Volim Mail 1.0 Build 135 — six fixes from real-account testing.\n\nMail:\n- Searching from inside Spam or Trash now shows results; the folder filter was cancelling itself out.\n- Notes you add to a conversation now show in the reading pane and persist with the account.\n- A scheduled message that matches one you sent in the last day no longer sits as \"failed\"; Send Now sends it. Scheduled \"Send & Archive\" now archives the thread once it goes out.\n- \"Request read receipt\" now actually asks for one.\n- Receipt scanning in Settings › Storage shows progress, can be cancelled, and can no longer hang on a slow AI backend.\n- Clicking a message selects it immediately instead of after a double-click delay.\n- Shift-click selects a range of messages and ⌘-click toggles one, like Gmail; Shift+↑\/↓ extends the selection.\n\nTesting note: every Pro feature is unlocked in this build and the upgrade prompt is disabled.\n\nThis early-access build is signed with the existing Apple Development identity and a separately signed update manifest. It is not notarized. Apple Developer ID distribution is deferred; first-time installation may require normal macOS approval. Existing installations use the signed GitHub update feed.\n\nThe update preserves existing mail data and settings.",
